  48: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  49:     """
  50:     Move each marker from a lattice corner gap into the adjacent enclosed 12-pixel cavity.
  51: 
  52:     Input structure:
  53:     - The grid is a repeated teal lattice around black 12-pixel cavities.
  54:     - A marker is a non-black pixel placed at the northwest corner gap of one
  55:       complete 5x5 lattice tile; the marker may itself be teal.
  56: 
  57:     Rule:
  58:     - For every marked northwest corner gap, clear that marker to black.
  59:     - Fill the 12 black pixels in the tile immediately down-right of the marker
  60:       with the marker color.
  61:     - Leave the rest of the lattice unchanged.
  62: 
  63:     Key insight:
  64:     - The apparent isolated markers are control pixels for the adjacent cavity;
  65:       teal markers are recognized as extra teal pixels occupying a gap that the
  66:       periodic lattice template says should be black.
  67:     """
